course: dictionary
lesson: 5457
title: One word, many lanes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Read the words around lane to find out. «He lies in the hedge by the dusty lane» means a narrow road in the countryside, because hedges and dust are clues.
explain: «a truck may turn across the inside lane at a junction» is different. Here lane means one strip of a road, for one line of cars. Cars stay in their lanes, and a bus lane is kept for buses.
explain: Lane can also be a strip of a race track or a swimming pool, for one runner or swimmer. In «sees an empty lane», the clue is a road where cars come from the right, so lane means a road strip there too. Always ask which meaning makes sense in the sentence.
fact: A lane is a narrow road, especially in the countryside.
fact: A lane is one strip of a road for one line of cars.
fact: A lane is one strip of a running track or swimming pool for one person.
fact: A lane in a bowling alley is the long wooden path the ball rolls down.
fact: Phrases with lane include bike lane, fast lane, slow lane, bus lane, change lanes and memory lane, which means memories of the past.
exercise: «He lies in the hedge by the dusty lane.» What kind of lane is this? | A swimming pool strip for one person | A bowling alley path | A narrow road in the countryside | *A narrow road, between hedges or fields
exercise: «a truck may turn across the inside lane at a junction» Which meaning fits? | A country road with hedges | A wooden path for a ball | *One strip of a road for one line of cars | A race track for runners
exercise: In a race, each swimmer has their own lane. Copy the word that means one strip of a swimming pool. | pool | race | *lane | swim
test: «Temporary traffic lights at roadworks take turns letting one direction of traffic through a single lane.» What does single lane mean here? | A lane for buses only | Two roads side by side | A bowling alley | *One strip of road for one line of traffic
test: Mill Lane is part of a street name in «Mill Lane and Station Road». What is Lane doing in that name? | It is a bus lane | *It is part of the name of a street | It means memories of the past | It is a swimming pool
exam: Which phrase means memories of the past? | bus lane | bike lane | fast lane | *memory lane
